{"toolCallId":"call_a235954e733f4a4bb4521e66744d181c","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Paths used below**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` and `P` is `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser and the final exit path in the script to confirm where the gate belongs (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'Unexpected argument' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the current text report for the packet folder as the parity baseline (`P/scratch/baseline.txt`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$P\" > \"$P/scratch/baseline.txt\"` exits 0 and the file is non-empty.\n- [ ] T003 Capture the current JSON report for the packet folder as the second baseline (`P/scratch/baseline.json`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json \"$P\" > \"$P/scratch/baseline.json\"` exits 0 and the file is non-empty.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global and a `--min-percent` branch that shifts two arguments (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\"` exits 0 and prints the normal report.\n- [ ] T005 Reject a value that is not a whole number with an `ERROR` line on stderr and exit 1, before analysis (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T006 Select the exit status from the completion value the report used, written as a full `if` so `set -e` does not exit early (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T007 Add `--min-percent <N>` to `show_help` and document exit `3` in the exit-code comment block (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints one line containing `--min-percent`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Prove text-output parity between a run with and without the option (`P/scratch/parity.txt`). Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T009 Prove JSON-output parity between a run with and without the option (`P/scratch/parity.json`). Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline.json\" <(bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 0 \"$P\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 Confirm the gate returns 0 at a threshold the report meets and 3 at one it cannot meet (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `0` and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T011 Record the parity and exit-status results in the packet summary (`P/implementation-summary.md`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent' \"$P/implementation-summary.md\"` prints at least one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `diff` of the baseline and the `--min-percent` run prints nothing for both text and `--json`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":15,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":20}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_a5df2ab5d9e94b55b4f38e546efa96be","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Paths used below**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` and `P` is `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser and the final exit path in the script to confirm where the gate belongs (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'Unexpected argument' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the current text report for the packet folder as the parity baseline (`P/scratch/baseline.txt`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$P\" > \"$P/scratch/baseline.txt\"` exits 0 and the file is non-empty.\n- [ ] T003 Capture the current JSON report for the packet folder as the second baseline (`P/scratch/baseline.json`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json \"$P\" > \"$P/scratch/baseline.json\"` exits 0 and the file is non-empty.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global and a `--min-percent` branch that shifts two arguments (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\"` exits 0 and prints the normal report.\n- [ ] T005 Reject a value that is not a whole number with an `ERROR` line on stderr and exit 1, before analysis (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T006 Select the exit status from the completion value the report used, written as a full `if` so `set -e` does not exit early (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T007 Add `--min-percent <N>` to `show_help` and document exit `3` in the exit-code comment block (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints one line containing `--min-percent`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Prove text-output parity between a run with and without the option (`P/scratch/parity.txt`). Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T009 Prove JSON-output parity between a run with and without the option (`P/scratch/parity.json`). Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline.json\" <(bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 0 \"$P\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 Confirm the gate returns 0 at a threshold the report meets and 3 at one it cannot meet (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `0` and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T011 Record the parity and exit-status results in the packet summary (`P/implementation-summary.md`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent' \"$P/implementation-summary.md\"` prints at least one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `diff` of the baseline and the `--min-percent` run prints nothing for both text and `--json`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path).` then `Verify:` and the command with the output it must print.\n\n**Paths used below**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` and `P` is `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the argument parser and the final exit path in the script to confirm where the gate belongs (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'Unexpected argument' \"$S\"` prints one line.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the current text report for the packet folder as the parity baseline (`P/scratch/baseline.txt`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$P\" > \"$P/scratch/baseline.txt\"` exits 0 and the file is non-empty.\n- [ ] T003 Capture the current JSON report for the packet folder as the second baseline (`P/scratch/baseline.json`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json \"$P\" > \"$P/scratch/baseline.json\"` exits 0 and the file is non-empty.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global and a `--min-percent` branch that shifts two arguments (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\"` exits 0 and prints the normal report.\n- [ ] T005 Reject a value that is not a whole number with an `ERROR` line on stderr and exit 1, before analysis (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `1`.\n- [ ] T006 Select the exit status from the completion value the report used, written as a full `if` so `set -e` does not exit early (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T007 Add `--min-percent <N>` to `show_help` and document exit `3` in the exit-code comment block (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints one line containing `--min-percent`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Prove text-output parity between a run with and without the option (`P/scratch/parity.txt`). Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T009 Prove JSON-output parity between a run with and without the option (`P/scratch/parity.json`). Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline.json\" <(bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 0 \"$P\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 Confirm the gate returns 0 at a threshold the report meets and 3 at one it cannot meet (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `0` and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$P\"; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T011 Record the parity and exit-status results in the packet summary (`P/implementation-summary.md`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent' \"$P/implementation-summary.md\"` prints at least one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `diff` of the baseline and the `--min-percent` run prints nothing for both text and `--json`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
